dialect protocol
protocol stdio.semio.brep.mutations
version 1
schema stdio.semio.brep
start body
framing record

# brep wave: REAL binary op frame, replacing the old `serde_json::to_vec`-of-the-whole-enum
# shortcut (`🧬️mutations/🦀️component.rs`'s old `OpBinary::encode_op`). `SemioBrepMutation` is a
# genuine data-carrying enum whose variants embed nested `BrepVertex`/`BrepEdge`/`BrepCurve`/
# `BrepSurface`/`SemioBrepSnapshot` payloads — no `dsl::DslField` impl exists for the tagged
# `BrepCurve`/`BrepSurface` enums (hand-rolled per this subset's own `🔺️diff`/`🧬️mutations`
# convention), so the generic derive-based `format u8 | ordinal varint | record body` layout
# doesn't apply. Handcrafted instead: `format u8` (`OP_BINARY_FORMAT` convention) + `tag u8` (the
# `SemioBrepMutation` variant ordinal, `🧬️mutations/🦀️component.rs`'s `OP_KEYWORDS`/
# `variant_ordinal`, same 0-22 ordering as `parse_brep_mutation`'s keyword match) as two REAL fixed
# fields, then the variant's own `key=value ...` argument payload as one opaque trailing `bytes`
# chain — the same honest boundary the sibling `../../🔺️diff/💾️binary/📡️component.protocol.semio`
# uses (`protocol-array-of-records`/`protocol-prim-ref-recursion`, per the recipe's gap table).
header fixed 2
field format u8
field tag u8

chain payload bytes
